[00:20.34] In these days of changing ways
[00:22.70] So called liberated days
[00:25.29] A story comes to mind of a friend of mine
[00:30.32] Georgie boy was gay I guess
[00:33.18] Nothin' more or nothin' less
[00:35.75] The kindest guy I ever knew
[00:40.32] His mother's tears fell in vain
[00:42.81] The afternoon George tried to explain
[00:45.72] That he needed love like all the rest
[00:50.49] Pa said there must be a mistake
[00:52.97] How can my son not be straight
[00:55.55] After all I've said and done for him
[01:00.31] 
[01:10.04] Leavin' home on a Greyhound bus
[01:12.52] Cast out by the ones he loves
[01:14.95] A victim of these gay days it seems
[01:20.19] 
[01:29.60] Georgie went to New York town
[01:32.28] Where he quickly settled down
[01:34.56] And soon became the toast of the great white way
[01:39.28] Accepted by Manhattan's elite
[01:41.84] In all the places that were chic
[01:43.98] No party was complete without George
[01:49.22] Along the boulevards he'd cruise
[01:51.75] And all the old queens blew a fuse
[01:54.26] Everybody loved Georgie boy
[01:58.96] 
[02:08.71] The last time I saw George alive
[02:11.25] Was in the summer of seventy-five
[02:13.75] He said he was in love I said I'm pleased
[02:18.63] George attended the opening night
[02:21.18] Of another Broadway hype
[02:23.24] But split before the final curtain fell
[02:28.20] Deciding to take a short cut home
[02:30.92] Arm in arm they meant no wrong
[02:33.24] A gentle breeze blew down Fifth Avenue
[02:37.85] 
[02:48.08] Out of a darkened side street came
[02:50.15] A New Jersey gang with just one aim
[02:52.63] To roll some innocent passer-by
[02:57.53] There ensued a fearful fight
[02:59.98] Screams rang out in the night
[03:02.45] Georgie's head hit a sidewalk cornerstone
[03:07.25] A leather kid, a switchblade knife
[03:09.67] He did not intend to take his life
[03:11.92] He just pushed his luck a little too far that night
[03:16.91] The sight of blood dispersed the gang
[03:19.41] A crowd gathered, the police came
[03:21.94] An ambulance screamed to a halt on Fifty-third and Third
[03:27.48] 
[03:36.46] Georgie's life ended there
[03:39.12] But I ask who really cares
[03:41.32] George once said to me and I quote
[03:45.93] He said, "Never wait or hesitate
[03:48.81] Get in kid, before it's too late
[03:51.27] You may never get another chance
[03:55.82] 'Cause youth's a mask but it don't last
[03:58.83] Live it long and live it fast"
